# Tag

A tag names a status. It is not an action.

These are civica reference implementations for component authors. They do not replace native Home Assistant behaviour or demonstrate a connection to a live home.

## State label or attention count

Use the [shared state vocabulary and message decision](status.html#choose-the-right-message). This page owns the rectangular, non-interactive status-label variant. Use the [notification badge](notification-badge.html) only for a count of new or unread items, and a [banner](notification-banners.html) when a complete message needs scope and an action. Do not turn a tag into any of those by changing its colour or adding a click handler.

## When to use it

Use a short status label when it helps people understand a device, task or record. Start with the smallest useful set of statuses and use the same vocabulary consistently.

## When not to use it

Do not put a link inside a tag or use a verb such as “Start” that suggests an action. Avoid giving every normal reading a prominent coloured label.

## Home Assistant adaptation

Distinguish “Unavailable” from “Off”: lack of a connection does not prove the physical state. A setup task may be “Completed” while the associated device is currently unavailable; these are different facts and need different labels.

## Accessibility and behaviour

Use sentence case and visible words. Colour is a secondary cue and uses semantic roles independent of the selected brand. Keep tags in the normal reading order and place any associated action separately.

